Latin Table
===========

TypingManiaNovel accepts letter-key input while lyrics may contain Japanese
kana, full-width characters, styled Latin characters, and display-only
symbols. This table, inherited from TypingMania NEO and maintained in this
repository, maps those characters to accepted Latin input sequences. It is
also the built-in Japanese kana/romaji implementation; no external
romanization service is contacted during play or QQ Music import.

`build-csv.js` can seed mapping CSV files, but the checked-in tables contain
carefully reviewed manual entries. Do not regenerate them without reviewing
the resulting diff.

Available mapping tables:

- `japanese-kana`: Hiragana and Katakana
- `japanese-kana-halfwidth`: half-width Katakana
- `cjk-symbols`: CJK symbols
- `full-width`: full-width Latin characters and symbols
- `enclosed-alnum`: enclosed alphanumerics and selected enclosed CJK forms
- `latin-extended`: Latin-1 Supplement and Latin Extended blocks
- `quote`: Unicode quotation marks

Notable rules include alternate kana input sequences, standalone small kana,
and special handling for `っ`, `ッ`, `ゝ`, `ゞ`, `ヽ`, and `ヾ`. Display-only
spacing and punctuation remain visible in lyrics but do not require a
keypress.
